`var` is function-scoped, so all three callbacks close over the same single `i`. `setTimeout` callbacks run only after the loop finishes, by which point `i` is 3 (the value that failed `i < 3`), so each callback logs 3.

Fix: use `let`, which creates a fresh binding per iteration:

```js
for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
  setTimeout(() => console.log(i), 0);
}
```

This prints 0 1 2. (The pre-ES6 fix was an IIFE or `setTimeout(console.log, 0, i)` to capture the current value.)
